# Sony libkernl syscall stubs (TU sdk/asm/klib), in link order.
#
# Each row is one stub: the syscall number, then the function name, then (optionally)
# the one disc that links it. scripts/klib.py turns this table into the assembly at
# build time; every stub has the same four instructions (number into $v1, syscall,
# return), the way PS2SDK generates its kernel stubs. Negative numbers are the
# interrupt-context (i...) entry points. Names are the Korean disc's symbols.
# Only names and numbers belong here: scripts/audit_repo.py rejects anything else.

